TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261215
SUMMARY:Deadline: Humboldt Residency Programme 2027\, "Oceanic Horizons: Th
 e Future of our Blue Planet" (funded six-week residency for researchers\, 
 creatives and practitioners)
DESCRIPTION:Each year the Humboldt Foundation brings twelve people from res
 earch\, the arts and civil society together to work on one topic and find 
 new ways of communicating it to audiences beyond academia. The 2027 topic 
 is Oceanic Horizons: The Future of our Blue Planet.\n\nOrganisation: Alexa
 nder von Humboldt Foundation\nLocation: Schloss Wiepersdorf (Brandenburg) 
 and Berlin\, Germany. In person. Researchers must be based outside Germany
 \; people from civil society\, journalism and the arts can apply from anyw
 here\, including Germany.\nAward: Monthly allowance for the six-week resid
 ency (figure not published: researchers get standard Humboldt fellowship r
 ates\, creatives and practitioners a competitive honorarium)\, travel allo
 wance to and from Germany\, accommodation at Schloss Wiepersdorf and a Ber
 lin aparthotel\, and a budget for public formats. No family allowance. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Virtual kick-off 29 June 2027\; residency 2 Au
 gust to 10 September 2027 (two weeks at Schloss Wiepersdorf\, four weeks i
 n Berlin)\; remote wrap-up to 26 October 2027\n\nMore: https://www.humbold
 t-foundation.de/en/apply/sponsorship-programmes/humboldt-residency-program
 me/humboldt-residency-programme-call-for-applications?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.humboldt-foundation.de/en/apply/sponsorship-programmes/humb
 oldt-residency-programme/humboldt-residency-programme-call-for-application
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Schloss Wiepersdorf (Brandenburg) and Berlin\, Germany. In person.
  Researchers must be based outside Germany\; people from civil society\, j
 ournalism and the arts can apply from anywhere\, including Germany.
END:VEVENT
